{title: Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer}
{artist: Johnny Marks}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 120}
{tags: Christmas, Kids, Fun, Secular}
{copyright: St. Nicholas Music Inc.}
{year: 1949}

{comment: Fun kids' song - upbeat and cheerful}

{start_of_verse}
[C]Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer
Had a very shiny [G]nose
And if you ever saw it
You would even say it [C]glows
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
[C]All of the other reindeer
Used to laugh and call him [G]names
They never let poor Rudolph
Join in any reindeer [C]games
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge}
[F]Then one foggy [C/E]Christmas Eve
[Dm]Santa came to [C]say
[G]"Rudolph, with your nose so bright
[D]Won't you guide my [G]sleigh tonight?"
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse}
[C]Then how the reindeer loved him
As they shouted out with [G]glee
"Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer
You'll go down in hist[C]ory"
{end_of_verse}
